\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Protocol evolution across rounds on the nine long-horizon and production-oriented benchmarks, one per row. Solid ovals are agent roles, pills inside a dashed container are internal phases of a single-agent solver, solid edges are admissible handoffs, and dashed edges are validity or retry edges. Boxed text pinned to an element is a transition or completion predicate, and the lower container holds the shared rule and culture. Elements introduced by the current round carry the color of their edit level from Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:self_evolving} and earlier elements are gray, so a round that leaves the graph unchanged still shows what it revised.}}{19}{figure.52}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:case_evo}{{6}{19}{Protocol evolution across rounds on the nine long-horizon and production-oriented benchmarks, one per row. Solid ovals are agent roles, pills inside a dashed container are internal phases of a single-agent solver, solid edges are admissible handoffs, and dashed edges are validity or retry edges. Boxed text pinned to an element is a transition or completion predicate, and the lower container holds the shared rule and culture. Elements introduced by the current round carry the color of their edit level from Section~\ref {sec:self_evolving} and earlier elements are gray, so a round that leaves the graph unchanged still shows what it revised}{figure.52}{}}
